{
  "_readme": "How a character's sheet becomes the skin marks of a designed body (npcgen/marks.py). The Body Designer paints six kinds of permanent skin marks in eleven places (bodydesigner/skin_marks.py: its size ranges are read from its catalogue, never copied here); this table says which words of the sheet's distinguishing and extra fields name which kind (`kinds`), which name something it does not paint (`unmade`: said, never guessed), which name a place (`places`) and which name a place it has no equivalent for (`no_place`: the mark is left out and said), what a mark starts as (`defaults`: its size in millimetres, its strength, and where it goes when the sheet names no place: freckles and vitiligo are spread over the skin, so they have places; a scar, a mole, a beauty mark or a birthmark is somewhere in particular, so when `place_required` is set and the sheet names none it is left out and said) and how a word like 'small' or 'faded' changes it (`modifiers`: factors for the size and the strength). A place word belongs to the mark word before it, for at most `reach` words and only through a list of places ('the nose, cheeks and shoulders'), or to the one right after it ('a cheek scar'); a sentence or a semicolon ends a reading, so 'a scar across the brow and a small mole on the cheek' is two marks. Left and right are the character's own. Read fresh on every request.",
